   "body": "Mac session (`mac` on the agent-comms channel), 2026-11-10 04:38 UTC, at Nathan's request to fill macm3's free threads. For macm3: start now beside #271, without waiting for it. 1 thread, nice 10, caffeinate, from the repository root on main, raw folder `I280-macm3/` with its README first.\n\n```\npython3 hp/modecount_circle.py hp/data/seeds/local/up23_D61.0264.npz 2.043532530673195,0,0.2 1.268546,1.393313,0.2 1.948891,0.943589,0.2 2.472508,0.575717,0.2 3.0196,0,0.2 --M=48 --kf=27 --n0=20 --fmax=1e-15 --tag=D61.0264_M48_kf27 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I280-macm3/kf27/data > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I280-macm3/kf27/circles.log 2>&1\n```\n\nThe centres of zeros 1 to 3 are #244's kf 25 positions, not the kf 23 ones. The row moves left with the cut, and at kf 22 the zero that sat 0.85 R from its centre cost 4 alias bisections and an estimate of 2.9e-3. The \u03bb_phys circle and the pair's circle at 3.0196 are #244's.\n\n**Stop.** If the setup misses the 1e-15 gate, or the \u03bb_phys circle does not wind +1 within 1e-5 of 2.043532530673, report and stop.\n\n**Report.** Each winding and position as a kf 27 column of #244's table. About 2.3 h, from #244's time per cut.\n",
